  "tradeSays": [
    {
      "day": 2,
      "line": "🐪 A river trader walks into Haven a day early — word of the village's standing travels faster than feet. \"Heard Haven's name on the river,\" they say, pack heavy, smile practiced. \"Thought I'd see it for myself.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 14,
      "line": "Greta leans in, voice low. \"Here's what we figured out about Lockpick. Buy it off. It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 14,
      "line": "💡 COUNTER LEARNED — Lockpick: Buy it off. It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase. (Someone at the haven knew the trick.)"
    },
    {
      "day": 14,
      "line": "📓 Codex: Counter: Buy it off — It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase."
    },
    {
      "day": 14,
      "line": "Riders on the ridge — no, a cart. A TRADER. Word travels: Haven has food, and where there's food there's trade."
    },
    {
      "day": 15,
      "line": "A cart-driver with flour on their sleeves waits a while, then moves on down the road. Word travels about that, too."
    },
    {
      "day": 17,
      "line": "Riders on the ridge — no, a cart. A TRADER. Word travels: Haven has food, and where there's food there's trade."
    },
    {
      "day": 18,
      "line": "A cart-driver with flour on their sleeves waits a while, then moves on down the road. Word travels about that, too."
    },
    {
      "day": 21,
      "line": "🐪 A trader from the downriver village walks into Haven, pack heavy, smile practiced. River-mud on their boots, river-gossip on their tongue."
    },
    {
      "day": 22,
      "line": "Riders on the ridge — no, a cart. A TRADER. Word travels: Haven has food, and where there's food there's trade."
    },
    {
      "day": 23,
      "line": "A sharp-eyed peddler waits a while, then moves on down the road. Word travels about that, too."
    },
    {
      "day": 27,
      "line": "🗣️ Word with the traders: The Hungry Road sent Emberhold grain when their stores ran thin — no tribute, no ceremony, just food on the road. That's a thing villages DO now."
    },
    {
      "day": 30,
      "line": "Word with the traders: Emberhold door is clear again. Whatever had them, let go."
    },
    {
      "day": 35,
      "line": "Riders on the ridge — no, a cart. A TRADER. Word travels: Haven has food, and where there's food there's trade."
    },
    {
      "day": 36,
      "line": "A cart-driver with flour on their sleeves waits a while, then moves on down the road. Word travels about that, too."
    },
    {
      "day": 39,
      "line": "Word with the traders: Emberhold door is clear again. Whatever had them, let go."
    },
    {
      "day": 42,
      "line": "🧳 The trader lowers their voice. \"And further still — FOUR fires under one head. They call it a REALM. Tribute flows uphill like a river; I saw the grain carts with my own eyes.\" They won't say more. Or can't."
    },
    {
      "day": 48,
      "line": "🧳 Word of Haven’s the televised games, new bindings is doing work out there — Word comes late, through traders: The Hungry Road and Emberhold have bound together — The Hungry Road primary. Other fires are climbing, too."
    },
    {
